toral Literacy Club\nProspectus Preparation Committee\nAnnual Assurance Report (AQAR) Committee\nContact Us\nContact Us\nResponsible money management also means setting clear boundaries for discretionary spending. Anyone choosing gambling as a form of entertainment can benefit from learning about\ncasino games for real money\nbefore deciding whether and how much to spend.\nLatest News-\nNotice for Sessional Examination_Odd Semester_Session 2026-2027\n,\nNotice for FYUGP BA 3rd & 5th Semester Admission_Session 2026-2027\n,\nAdmission Commitee Meeting FYUGP (Non-CUET) Spot Admission_Minutes of the Meeting\nEdit Template\nNotice |\nAll Notice\nNOtice for Sessional Examination Programme for Odd Semester_session 2026-2027\n2026-09-10\nView File\nAdmission Notice for FYUGP B.A. 3rd & 5th Semester_Session 2026-2027\n2026-08-03\nView File\nRegistration for Admission in B.A. (FYUGP) 1st Semester_Session 2026-27\n2026-04-10\nView File\nNotice for Sessional Examination NOtice_Session 2025- 2026\n2026-03-30\nView File\nNotice for B.A. 4th Semester_Geography Department (Major & Minor) Field Study Notification\n2026-03-25\nView File\nNotice for B.A. 2nd Semester Subject Selection in SAMARTH Portal\n2026-03-12\nView File\nTDC CBCS EVEN SEMESTER FORM FILL UP NOTIFICATION\n2026-03-09\nView File\nNotice For B.A. 6th Semester (FYUGP) Course Selection\n2026-03-06\nView File\nNotice for B.A. 2nd Semester Boys Students\n2026-02-24\nView File\nNotification of Photo upload in the Samarth student profile and guidelines)\n2026-02-20\nView File\nFYUGP 3rd Semester Course Registration 2025)\n2025-11-05\nView File\nB.A. 3rd Semester (FYUGP) Final Examination Programme 2025)\n2025-11-04\nView File\nNotice for B.A. 1st Semester (CBCS) Arrear Final Examination Programme\n2025-10-27\nView File\nNotice for B.A. 3rd Semester (CBCS) Arrear Final Examination Programme\n2025-10-27\nView File\nNotice for B.A. 5th Semester (CBCS) Arrear Final Examination Programme\n2025-10-27\nView File\nNotice for B.A. 5th Semester (FYUGP) regarding Internship\n2025-10-23\nView File\nSessional Examination Programme for B.A. Students\n2025-10-16\nView File\nExamination form fill up of B.A. TDC (CBCS) Semester- I (Arrear Batches 2020 & 2021), Semester- II (Arrear Batches 2020 & 2021) and Semester_ V (Arrear Batches 2020 & 2021)\n2025-10-08\nView File\nSessional Examination Notification for B.A. Students\n2025-10-07\nView File\nUser Manual on Applying for Scholarship through Student Login\n2025-10-07\nView File\nSecond Merit List, FYUGP_B.A. First Semester Admission, Session 2025- 2026\n2025-06-12\nView File\n2024-02-17\nView File\nAbout The College\nDeomornoi is a place of immense historical significance located in the North Western part of the Darrang district, Assam. Nestled approximately 15 kilometers away from Mangaldai town, Deomornoi has been an integral part of the region’s cultural and educational landscape. Recognizing the need for a higher education institution in the area, the residents came together during the early nineties to establish Deomornoi Degree College in 1993.\nRead More\nThe primary objective of Deomornoi Degree College is to provide quality higher education to aspiring students. Situated near the renowned Siala Vaishnab Temple, the college enjoys a picturesque setting on the banks of the historically significant Mornoi river. The sprawling college campus spans across 25 bighas of land and boasts essential infrastructural facilities.\nCurrently, the college caters to a student population of over 1084, supported by a dedicated staff of forty-six employees. Deomornoi Degree College has earned the prestigious permanent affiliation from Gauhati University. As a result, it has been granted permission to offer major courses in nearly all subjects of the arts stream. Additionally, the college provides Computer Application as a vocational subject, ensuring that students are equipped with practical skills aligned with the demands of the digital age.\nIn its pursuit of academic excellence, Deomornoi Degree College has also established a contact center for M.A. courses in various disciplines under the Institute of Distance and Open Learning (IDOL) at Gauhati University. This initiative enables students to pursue higher education and specialization in their chosen fields, further expanding their knowledge and career prospects.\nDeomornoi Degree College stands as a beacon of education in the region, empowering students to strive for intellectual growth, holistic development, and a bright future. With its commitment to quality education and a nurturing environment, the college continues to contribute significantly to the educational landscape of the Darrang district and beyond.\nFrom The Principal's Desk\nDr. Gitali Kalita\nLatest News |\nView All\nNotice for Session Examination_Odd Semester_Session 2026- 2027\nNotice for B.A. 4th Semester (FYUGP) Geography Department (Major & Minor) Field Study Notification\nNotice for B.A. 2nd Semester (FYUGP) Course/ Subject Selection in SAMARTH Portal\nTDC CBCS EVEN SEMESTER FORM FILL UP NOTIFICATION\nNotice and Guidelines for B.A. 6th Semester (FYUGP)_Course Selection on SAMARTH Portal\nNotice for B.A. 2nd Semester Boys Students\nNotification of Photo upload in the Samarth student profile and guidelines\nGauhati University Holiday List_2026\nPhoto Gallery |\nView All\nOnline Portal Links\nOnline Admission\nSamarth Portal\nDCS Portal Link\nClick Here For Prospectus\nGauhati University SAMARTH Registration Portal\nSWAYAM\nAcademic Bank of Credits\nGallery\nUseful Links\nGuwahati University\nDibrugarh University\nTezpur University\nUGC\nSEBA\nAHSEC\nIDOL\nKKHSOU\nQuick Links\nGallery\nNotice\nTenders\nCopyright © 2024 Deomornoi Degree College\nScroll to Top", "links": [{"label": "Skip to content", "url": "https://deomornoidegreecollege.com/#content"}, {"label": "Deomornoi Degree College", "url": "https://deomornoidegreecollege.com"}, {"label": "Home", "url": "https://deomornoidegreecollege.com/"}, {